nd Construction Faculty Faculty and Teaching Faculty Development Genetics Grants Administration & Sponsored Programs Health and Medical Services Human Resources Information Technology Information Technology Services Institutional Research and Planning Keck Medicine of USC Laboratory Laboratory and Research Legal Services Marketing and Events Nursing Nursing Services Pharmacy Physician Assistant Postdoctoral Public Safety Research and Clinical Support Research and Grants Administration Social Work Speech Therapy Student Support Services Support Services Technician Therapy and Rehabilitation USC Job Families School/Division Select One Keck Medicine of USC Keck School of Medicine Auxiliary Services Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry of USC Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry Sol Price School of Public Policy Enrollment Services Marshall School of Business Keck School of Medicine of USC Viterbi School of Engineering Alfred E. Mann School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences USC Credit Union Facilities Management Services University Relations Gould School of Law Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance Communications Office of the Provost School of Architecture Administrative Operations Information Technology Services SOWK USC Keck School of Medicine Annenberg School for Communication and Journalism Athletics Bovard College Office of Research Capital Construction Dworak-Peck School of Social Work Financial and Business Services Kaufman School of Dance Leonard Davis School of Gerontology Office of the General Counsel Rossier School of Education School of Cinematic Arts Global and Online Initiatives Keck School Of Medicine Libraries Office of the Comptroller President Roski School of Art and Design Thornton School of Music USC Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences University Advancement Add Remove Confirm Email By signing up, I acknowledge I have read the USC privacy policy , and I wish to receive email and SMS communications. I understand I can opt-out from receiving email and SMS communications at any time. sign up Helpful information for applicants External applicants Internal applicants (current USC employees) Employment Equity Read USC's Clery Act Annual Security Report Recruitment Fraud Alert Labor Condition Applications Sitemap Equal Opportunity Statement USC is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. USC observes affirmative action obligations consistent with state and federal law. USC will consider for employment all qualified applicants with criminal records in a manner consistent with applicable laws and regulations, including the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for employers and the Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, and with due consideration for patient and student safety. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants with questions about access or requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact USC Human Resources by phone at (213) 821-8100, or by email at uschr@usc.edu . Inquiries will be treated as confidential to the extent permitted by law. Interested in working for USC on a temporary basis? Contact Trojan Talent Source (operated by Kelly Services) at (800) 409-1066 or 15HD@kellyservices.com . Copyright © 2026 University of Southern California Privacy Notice Digital Accessibility Notice of Non-Discrimination Smoke-Free Policy Cookie Policy X A message from USC Talent Acquisition: Please be aware that USC employment offers are only made in writing by authorized university officials, and only after an applicant has completed the online application. Merely sending an email does not constitute an application, and any offer of employment received before an applicant completes the online application is not authorized or valid. If you suspect you are being contacted by an unauthorized recruiter, please email your concerns to uschr@usc.edu ."
    },
    "https://employees.usc.edu/help-for-usc-job-applicants/": {
      "title": "FAQ for USC Applicants",
      "description": "FAQ for USC Applicants - Employee Gateway Skip to main content Go to usc.edu homepage USC Monogram Employee Gateway Menu An icon that consists of three parallel horizontal lines suggestive of a list. Home Work & life Show submenu for Work & life Onboarding Campus access and safety Getting paid HR contacts Life events USC systems Community resources for emergency response support Workplace information Leaving USC Benefits & perks Learn & grow Show submenu for Learn & grow Career development Learning and professional trainings Performance management USC applicant resources News & events Show submenu for News & events Events News Newsletters Research participation opportunities Community & recognition Show submenu for Community & recognition Our trojan veterans Trojan Spotlight staff recognition program Top Notch Trojans Volunteer opportunities Contact HR More… Show More Menu Search An icon of a magnifying glass. Search for: Close An icon of a letter X. Home Learn and Grow USC applicant resources FAQ for USC Applicants FAQ for USC Applicants Application process How can I check the status of my application at USC? Log in to your application profile and review the current status. If it states, “Under Review,” your application is still under consideration. Do I need a resume or cover letter for my application? Refer to the specific job posting on the USC Careers website to determine if a resume or cover letter is required for the position. Where can I upload a cover letter or additional document? Use the “upload” button in the same section where you attach your resume to add additional documents. Upload any relevant documents that may aid in considering your application in this section. How can I ask questions about a position listed on the USC Careers website? To receive assistance, please reach out to our HR Service Center and provide them with the requisition number on the job announcement. Can I get a copy of a job description/posting? You can find job descriptions for positions that you have applied to in your candidate account. If you are interested in learning more about other opportunities available at USC, visit the USC Careers website . How can I contact the hiring manager/recruiter for a position? A recruiter will contact you directly, if after reviewing your application you are identified as a candidate for the position. If you have any questions, contact the HR Service Center . Where can I find the salary range for positions? Salary ranges are posted on each job announcement. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. What if I need an accommodation to apply for a position? Please contact our HR Service Center and an associate will be available to assist you with obtaining reasonable accommodations during the application or hiring process. What should I do if the position I am interested in is no longer accepting applications? Positions may close after the minimum posting period is reached or when the requisition has received enough applications. We encourage you to check back to the USC Careers website often and apply to positions as soon as they become available. What should I do if my application is declined and I want feedback? Due to the high volume of interest and applications that USC receives, we are unable to provide direct feedback to applicants. We thank you for your interest and encourage you to visit the USC Careers website to continue exploring opportunities. How does USC ensure the confidentiality of my application? Candidate applications are reviewed only by authorized personnel involved in the hiring process. Application technical support Can I change my email address in the application system? Yes, you can change your email address through your applicant home menu by clicking on the cloud icon, choosing “account settings,” and validating your new email address. I forgot my username/password. How can I reset it? Contact our HR Service Center and provide them with your request, your name, and your email address. How can I reactivate my accidentally withdrawn application? Contact our HR Service Center and an associate can help to reactivate your application. What if I’m experiencing a technical issue with the application system that isn’t listed here? Contact our HR Service Center and an associate will be happy to assist you. Recruitment process How can I address questions about interview scheduling, employment screens, or offer letters? Contact our HR Service Center and provide the requisition number which you can find at the bottom of the job announcement. Are employment screens performed for all new employees? Yes, employment screens are conducted following a conditional offer of employment. Refer to USC’s background screening policy for details. Other job opportunity-related questions Does USC have temporary work opportunities? To explore work at USC on a temporary basis, please contact Trojan Talent Source (operated by Kelly Services) at 800-409-1066 or 15HD@kellyservices.com . Does USC have internships/volunteer opportunities? USC offers internships and volunteer opportunities. USC students can visit Handshake , and non-USC students should contact specific schools and/or units for information. How does USC handle work visa/sponsorship inquiries? At USC, visa sponsorship is evaluated on a case-by-case basis. If you are selected for an interview, notify the recruiter of your need for visa sponsorship. You can create a ticket with the HR Service Center . For all other questions related to applying for a job at USC, please contact our HR Service Center at uschr@usc.edu or 213-821-8100 Monday through Friday between 8 a.m. and 5 p.m. PT. Career development Career development toolkit Know yourself Career exploration Chart your course Career resources Learning and professional trainings Required training Coaching program Toastmasters at USC Performance management Keck USC competency performance statements – staff Keck USC competency performance statements – managers USC applicant resources Career growth opportunities Employee referral program Veteran referral program FAQ for USC Applicants USC HR, Ethics, and Compliance University Policy Emergency Information Notice of Non-Discrimination Report & Response Jobs at USC for Current Employees Jobs at USC for External Applicants LCA Postings University of Southern California Send website feedback to gateway@usc.edu Privacy Notice Digital Accessibility Notice of Non-Discrimination Smoke-Free Policy YouTube YouTube The logo for video sharing platform YouTube. Facebook Facebook The logo for the social media platform Facebook. Linkedin LinkedIn The logo for the social media platform LinkedIn."
    },
